1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,870
What’s today’s video about? We’ve got four exciting themes!

2
00:00:08,870 --> 00:00:10,370
Scene 1: Popular Japanese Cultural Experiences for Foreigners

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:13,570
Did you catch the morning news?

4
00:00:13,592 --> 00:00:16,159
No, I didn’t.

5
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,463
What was the news about?

6
00:00:18,487 --> 00:00:24,454
Japanese cultural experience tours are a big hit with foreigners!

7
00:00:24,477 --> 00:00:26,930
Cultural experience tours?

8
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:29,961
What kind of experiences are popular?

9
00:00:29,984 --> 00:00:34,864
Sushi-making and kimono-wearing experiences are really popular.

10
00:00:34,887 --> 00:00:36,821
That sounds like fun!

11
00:00:36,844 --> 00:00:40,298
Where can I try these experiences?

12
00:00:40,321 --> 00:00:44,380
You can experience them in Asakusa or Kyoto.

13
00:00:44,404 --> 00:00:48,537
Can I get guidance in English?

14
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:49,643
Yes, you can!

15
00:00:49,667 --> 00:00:53,500
English-speaking guides will help you out.

16
00:00:53,523 --> 00:00:57,523
That takes away any language worries!

17
00:00:57,546 --> 00:01:01,482
You get to eat the sushi you make right on the spot.

18
00:01:01,505 --> 00:01:05,712
Sushi you make yourself tastes amazing!

19
00:01:05,736 --> 00:01:09,669
There are also wagashi (Japanese sweets) making and tea ceremony classes.

20
00:01:09,692 --> 00:01:13,459
Making wagashi sounds really interesting too!

21
00:01:13,482 --> 00:01:16,728
You can enjoy them with matcha.

22
00:01:16,751 --> 00:01:20,328
You’ll be able to take lots of photos!

23
00:01:20,351 --> 00:01:21,845
Yes, you can!

24
00:01:21,868 --> 00:01:25,606
They’re super popular because they make such great memories.

25
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:28,709
How do I make a reservation?

26
00:01:28,732 --> 00:01:32,407
You can book online.

27
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:35,681
Can I book on the same day?

28
00:01:35,705 --> 00:01:40,772
Since they’re so popular, it’s best to book at least three days in advance.

29
00:01:40,795 --> 00:01:43,361
How much does it cost?

30
00:01:43,384 --> 00:01:48,118
It’s around 4,000 to 6,000 yen per person.

31
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:51,374
Can I pay with a credit card?

32
00:01:51,397 --> 00:01:53,000
Yes, you can!

33
00:01:53,023 --> 00:01:56,292
You can pay online in advance.

34
00:01:56,315 --> 00:01:59,999
What if I have allergies?

35
00:02:00,023 --> 00:02:04,995
You can specify that when you book, so no worries!

36
00:02:05,019 --> 00:02:07,893
I’d love to go with my family!

37
00:02:07,917 --> 00:02:12,150
Kids and adults can enjoy it together!

38
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:16,106
Do they offer traditional craft experiences like painting wind chimes?

39
00:02:16,129 --> 00:02:17,663
Yes, you can!

40
00:02:17,686 --> 00:02:21,619
Yes! You can paint designs on glass wind chimes.

41
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:25,381
That would make a great souvenir for myself!

42
00:02:25,404 --> 00:02:29,338
It’ll be a one-of-a-kind original piece!

43
00:02:29,361 --> 00:02:32,930
I’ll add this experience to my plans for this weekend!

44
00:02:32,954 --> 00:02:38,087
You can pick up brochures at tourist information centers.

45
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:41,110
I’ll head to the information desk at the station.

46
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:44,899
They also have QR codes for the website at the info centers.

47
00:02:44,922 --> 00:02:47,856
I’ll scan it with my phone and make a reservation.

48
00:02:47,879 --> 00:02:51,937
Enjoy lots of Japanese cultural experiences!

49
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,493
Thanks so much for all the details!

50
00:02:55,516 --> 00:02:58,350
Hope you have an amazing trip!

51
00:02:58,373 --> 00:02:59,828
Yes, you can!

52
00:02:59,851 --> 00:03:02,385
I’m really looking forward to the cultural experiences!

53
00:03:02,408 --> 00:03:11,417
You can download today’s video script from the description or top comment. Don’t forget to leave a comment before downloading!

54
00:03:11,417 --> 00:03:12,917
Scene 2: Sushi Making Experience Reservation

55
00:03:12,917 --> 00:03:14,983
Excuse me.

56
00:03:15,006 --> 00:03:19,464
I'd like to book a sushi-making experience.

57
00:03:19,488 --> 00:03:21,521
Welcome!

58
00:03:21,544 --> 00:03:25,783
Welcome to our sushi-making workshop!

59
00:03:25,807 --> 00:03:29,857
Do you have any openings for tomorrow's class?

60
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,447
Yes, you can!

61
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:35,514
Yes, we have availability in tomorrow's morning class.

62
00:03:35,537 --> 00:03:38,604
What time does it start?

63
00:03:38,628 --> 00:03:42,161
It starts at 10:00 AM.

64
00:03:42,184 --> 00:03:46,517
How long is the class?

65
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:51,075
The experience lasts about an hour and a half.

66
00:03:51,099 --> 00:03:54,233
We'd like to join as two people.

67
00:03:54,256 --> 00:03:56,622
For two, correct?

68
00:03:56,645 --> 00:03:59,379
We can take your reservation.

69
00:03:59,402 --> 00:04:02,852
Do you have an English-speaking guide?

70
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:04,441
Yes, you can!

71
00:04:04,464 --> 00:04:08,523
An English-speaking staff member will assist with the class.

72
00:04:08,547 --> 00:04:12,627
What kinds of sushi can we make?

73
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:17,484
You'll learn to make nigiri and maki sushi.

74
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:20,956
How many pieces will we make?

75
00:04:20,979 --> 00:04:26,946
You'll prepare 8 pieces of nigiri and 1 roll of maki.

76
00:04:26,969 --> 00:04:30,335
That’s quite a lot!

77
00:04:30,358 --> 00:04:32,358
I’m really looking forward to it!

78
00:04:32,381 --> 00:04:37,228
You’ll get to eat the sushi you make right away!

79
00:04:37,252 --> 00:04:41,618
My friend has a shrimp allergy.

80
00:04:41,641 --> 00:04:43,616
Understood.

81
00:04:43,639 --> 00:04:48,073
We can substitute the shrimp with another topping.

82
00:04:48,096 --> 00:04:52,429
Can we switch it to salmon or tuna?

83
00:04:52,452 --> 00:04:53,985
Yes, you can!

84
00:04:54,008 --> 00:04:58,042
We’ll replace it with salmon or tamagoyaki (sweet egg).

85
00:04:58,065 --> 00:05:01,431
Thank you for your kind assistance.

86
00:05:01,454 --> 00:05:05,221
Please feel free to join with peace of mind.

87
00:05:05,244 --> 00:05:08,777
Do we need to bring anything?

88
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:13,835
We provide free aprons and hats.

89
00:05:13,859 --> 00:05:17,026
So we can come empty-handed!

90
00:05:17,049 --> 00:05:18,649
That’s great!

91
00:05:18,672 --> 00:05:22,672
Please make sure to wash your hands before joining.

92
00:05:22,695 --> 00:05:25,266
How much is the fee?

93
00:05:25,289 --> 00:05:29,558
It’s 4,500 yen per person.

94
00:05:29,581 --> 00:05:32,630
So that’s 9,000 yen for two.

95
00:05:32,653 --> 00:05:34,253
Yes, you can!

96
00:05:34,276 --> 00:05:36,749
The total comes to 9,000 yen.

97
00:05:36,772 --> 00:05:42,017
Can I pay with a credit card?

98
00:05:42,041 --> 00:05:43,607
Yes, you can!

99
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:48,364
We accept all major cards and contactless payments.

100
00:05:48,387 --> 00:05:51,477
I’ll pay now.

101
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:53,833
Here’s my card.

102
00:05:53,856 --> 00:05:57,689
Please tap your card on this machine.

103
00:05:57,712 --> 00:06:00,846
It beeped!

104
00:06:00,869 --> 00:06:03,602
Your payment is complete.

105
00:06:03,625 --> 00:06:06,636
Here’s your reservation voucher.

106
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:11,638
We’ll be there at 9:45 AM tomorrow.

107
00:06:11,661 --> 00:06:13,157
Yes, you can!

108
00:06:13,181 --> 00:06:17,233
Please arrive at our Asakusa workshop 15 minutes early.

109
00:06:17,256 --> 00:06:20,937
Is it close to Kaminarimon Gate?

110
00:06:20,961 --> 00:06:25,161
It’s just a 3-minute walk from Kaminarimon.

111
00:06:25,184 --> 00:06:27,801
That’s easy to find!

112
00:06:27,825 --> 00:06:30,658
I'm looking forward to tomorrow!

113
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,135
Yes, you can!

114
00:06:32,158 --> 00:06:34,657
We'll be waiting for you tomorrow.

115
00:06:34,681 --> 00:06:41,786
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment! *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

116
00:06:41,786 --> 00:06:43,286
Scene 3: Kimono Rental Basics

117
00:06:43,286 --> 00:06:45,125
Excuse me.

118
00:06:45,148 --> 00:06:47,841
I'd like to rent a kimono.

119
00:06:47,864 --> 00:06:49,506
Welcome!

120
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:52,863
Welcome to our kimono rental shop!

121
00:06:52,886 --> 00:06:55,919
Can I wear it now?

122
00:06:55,942 --> 00:06:57,410
Yes,

123
00:06:57,434 --> 00:07:00,600
you can rent without a reservation.

124
00:07:00,623 --> 00:07:03,300
What plans do you have?

125
00:07:03,324 --> 00:07:07,740
We offer a Standard Plan and a Premium Plan.

126
00:07:07,764 --> 00:07:10,142
What's the difference?

127
00:07:10,165 --> 00:07:15,931
The Premium Plan offers a wider selection of kimonos to choose from.

128
00:07:15,954 --> 00:07:18,521
I'll go with the Premium Plan.

129
00:07:18,544 --> 00:07:20,477
Understood.

130
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:24,667
Please choose your kimono from this rack.

131
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:27,823
There are so many patterns!

132
00:07:27,846 --> 00:07:29,688
Which one do you like?

133
00:07:29,712 --> 00:07:36,324
Since it's summer, I recommend lightweight kimonos or yukatas made from cool fabrics.

134
00:07:36,347 --> 00:07:40,514
I'd like this pink kimono with the cherry blossom pattern.

135
00:07:40,537 --> 00:07:43,382
That's a beautiful kimono!

136
00:07:43,405 --> 00:07:45,840
It'll look great on you.

137
00:07:45,863 --> 00:07:48,797
Can I choose an obi as well?

138
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,157
Yes,

139
00:07:50,181 --> 00:07:55,015
Please pick your favorite color from these obi options.

140
00:07:55,037 --> 00:07:57,248
I'll go with the yellow obi.

141
00:07:57,272 --> 00:08:00,806
Let me show you to the dressing room.

142
00:08:00,829 --> 00:08:04,122
How long does the dressing take?

143
00:08:04,145 --> 00:08:08,594
The dressing process takes about 20 minutes.

144
00:08:08,617 --> 00:08:12,422
Can I also get my hair styled?

145
00:08:12,446 --> 00:08:13,818
Yes,

146
00:08:13,842 --> 00:08:17,975
Hair styling is available for an additional 1,500 yen.

147
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:20,465
I'd like the hair styling as well, please.

148
00:08:20,488 --> 00:08:24,321
You can also choose a hair accessory for free!

149
00:08:24,344 --> 00:08:27,378
I'll take the red flower hair accessory.

150
00:08:27,401 --> 00:08:29,379
How cute!

151
00:08:29,402 --> 00:08:32,569
Your dressing and hair styling are complete.

152
00:08:32,592 --> 00:08:36,125
Wow, I look amazing!

153
00:08:36,148 --> 00:08:38,182
That’s great!

154
00:08:38,205 --> 00:08:42,282
Please check yourself out in the full-length mirror.

155
00:08:42,305 --> 00:08:46,972
Can I store my personal clothes and large luggage here?

156
00:08:46,995 --> 00:08:48,266
Yes,

157
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:52,898
We can store them in this large bag for you.

158
00:08:52,922 --> 00:08:56,021
I'll just carry my valuables with me.

159
00:08:56,045 --> 00:08:59,703
Please choose a drawstring bag and geta sandals.

160
00:08:59,726 --> 00:09:03,361
I'll take the black drawstring bag and red geta.

161
00:09:03,385 --> 00:09:06,352
You're all set to go out!

162
00:09:06,375 --> 00:09:10,592
What time do I need to return by?

163
00:09:10,615 --> 00:09:14,903
Please return to the shop by 5:30 PM.

164
00:09:14,926 --> 00:09:17,213
5:30 PM, got it.

165
00:09:17,237 --> 00:09:19,005
Understood.

166
00:09:19,028 --> 00:09:23,482
Late returns will incur an additional fee.

167
00:09:23,506 --> 00:09:26,153
I'll make sure to return on time.

168
00:09:26,176 --> 00:09:30,260
The total amount is 6,500 yen.

169
00:09:30,284 --> 00:09:33,151
Can I pay with PayPay?

170
00:09:33,174 --> 00:09:34,708
Yes,

171
00:09:34,731 --> 00:09:37,697
Please scan the QR code.

172
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,574
Payment completed.

173
00:09:39,598 --> 00:09:43,365
Enjoy your stroll around Kiyomizu-dera!

174
00:09:43,388 --> 00:09:46,258
I’ll take lots of photos!

175
00:09:46,281 --> 00:09:48,161
Have a wonderful time!

176
00:09:48,185 --> 00:09:49,685
Scene 4: Japanese Wagashi Making Experience

177
00:09:49,685 --> 00:09:51,818
Excuse me.

178
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:55,408
Is this the reception for the wagashi-making experience?

179
00:09:55,431 --> 00:09:58,450
Yes, this is the place.

180
00:09:58,474 --> 00:10:01,007
Welcome!

181
00:10:01,030 --> 00:10:05,208
I’m Maria, and I have a reservation for 11 o’clock.

182
00:10:05,231 --> 00:10:07,365
Maria, correct?

183
00:10:07,388 --> 00:10:09,924
We’ve been expecting you.

184
00:10:09,947 --> 00:10:13,714
What kind of wagashi will we make today?

185
00:10:13,737 --> 00:10:18,070
We’ll make two seasonal *nerikiri* sweets.

186
00:10:18,093 --> 00:10:20,832
What’s *nerikiri*?

187
00:10:20,855 --> 00:10:25,222
It’s a beautiful Japanese sweet made with red bean paste.

188
00:10:25,245 --> 00:10:29,421
Can we shape it by hand?

189
00:10:29,444 --> 00:10:34,503
Yes, we’ll use your palms and wooden molds to shape them.

190
00:10:34,527 --> 00:10:39,160
I’ve never done this before—will I be able to make them well?

191
00:10:39,183 --> 00:10:44,950
Of course! I’ll guide you step by step, so don’t worry.

192
00:10:44,973 --> 00:10:49,006
Do I need to wear an apron?

193
00:10:49,029 --> 00:10:54,396
Yes, please put on this apron and triangular cloth.

194
00:10:54,419 --> 00:10:57,085
I’ve put on the apron.

195
00:10:57,108 --> 00:10:59,442
I’ll wash my hands now.

196
00:10:59,465 --> 00:11:03,738
Please wash your hands thoroughly with soap.

197
00:11:03,762 --> 00:11:05,695
I’ve washed my hands.

198
00:11:05,718 --> 00:11:07,918
All set!

199
00:11:07,941 --> 00:11:10,775
Please have a seat here.

200
00:11:10,798 --> 00:11:12,865
I’ve prepared the tools.

201
00:11:12,888 --> 00:11:16,688
There are so many colors of red bean paste!

202
00:11:16,711 --> 00:11:20,406
We’ll roll pink and green bean paste into balls.

203
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:23,563
Can I roll them into perfect spheres?

204
00:11:23,586 --> 00:11:27,419
Just gently roll them in your palms.

205
00:11:27,442 --> 00:11:30,209
They turned out beautifully round!

206
00:11:30,232 --> 00:11:35,503
Next, use this wooden tool to add petal lines.

207
00:11:35,527 --> 00:11:38,422
So we’re adding veins to the petals?

208
00:11:38,446 --> 00:11:40,379
Let’s draw the lines.

209
00:11:40,402 --> 00:11:42,402
That looks amazing!

210
00:11:42,425 --> 00:11:45,564
A morning glory flower—done!

211
00:11:45,587 --> 00:11:50,231
Wow, it looks just like a real flower—so beautiful!

212
00:11:50,254 --> 00:11:54,067
For the second one, we’ll make a chrysanthemum.

213
00:11:54,090 --> 00:11:58,324
I did a great job shaping the second one too!

214
00:11:58,347 --> 00:12:02,980
Now, let’s whisk some matcha with this bamboo whisk.

215
00:12:03,003 --> 00:12:06,003
We’ll froth it up with a *shaka-shaka* motion.

216
00:12:06,026 --> 00:12:10,093
Use your wrist to move it quickly.

217
00:12:10,116 --> 00:12:12,735
It’s foamed up nicely!

218
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:17,559
Please enjoy your handmade wagashi with this matcha.

219
00:12:17,582 --> 00:12:20,415
We’ll cut it with this *kuromoji* pick.

220
00:12:20,438 --> 00:12:22,771
It’s sweet and delicious!

221
00:12:22,794 --> 00:12:27,131
The bitterness of the matcha pairs perfectly with the sweet wagashi.

222
00:12:27,155 --> 00:12:31,822
Can I take the remaining wagashi home?

223
00:12:31,845 --> 00:12:33,281
Yes,

224
00:12:33,304 --> 00:12:38,162
You can take it home in this special box.

225
00:12:38,186 --> 00:12:40,837
I'd love to show it to my family.

226
00:12:40,861 --> 00:12:42,957
I'll put it in the box for you.

227
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:48,213
The fee is 3,500 yen, which covers the experience and tea.

228
00:12:48,236 --> 00:12:50,731
I'll pay in cash.

229
00:12:50,754 --> 00:12:53,288
I'll give you 4,000 yen.

230
00:12:53,311 --> 00:12:55,799
Here's your 500 yen change.

231
00:12:55,823 --> 00:12:58,098
Thank you very much!

232
00:12:58,122 --> 00:12:59,622
Scene 5: Edo Furin Wind Chime Painting Experience

233
00:12:59,622 --> 00:13:01,955
Excuse me.

234
00:13:01,978 --> 00:13:05,822
I'd like to try painting a wind chime.

235
00:13:05,845 --> 00:13:07,934
Welcome!

236
00:13:07,958 --> 00:13:12,158
Welcome to our Edo wind chime shop!

237
00:13:12,181 --> 00:13:16,356
Can I try the experience without a reservation?

238
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,113
Yes,

239
00:13:18,136 --> 00:13:23,954
We're available now, so you can start right away!

240
00:13:23,977 --> 00:13:28,144
What kind of wind chime would you like to paint?

241
00:13:28,168 --> 00:13:33,044
You'll be painting on a plain, transparent glass wind chime.

242
00:13:33,067 --> 00:13:36,634
Will you paint on the inside

243
00:13:36,657 --> 00:13:39,257
or the outside?

244
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:44,951
You'll be painting on the inside of the wind chime with a brush.

245
00:13:44,974 --> 00:13:49,945
Painting from the inside? That sounds a bit tricky.

246
00:13:49,969 --> 00:13:55,636
You'll need to paint letters and images in reverse.

247
00:13:55,659 --> 00:14:00,592
Painting in reverse is a bit challenging.

248
00:14:00,615 --> 00:14:05,220
Don't worry, we have simple examples to guide you.

249
00:14:05,244 --> 00:14:08,530
What designs are popular?

250
00:14:08,554 --> 00:14:14,521
Goldfish, fireworks, and morning glories are very popular.

251
00:14:14,544 --> 00:14:17,977
I'd like to paint a red goldfish.

252
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,440
That's a wonderful summer-themed design!

253
00:14:21,464 --> 00:14:24,934
Do we use acrylic paint?

254
00:14:24,957 --> 00:14:26,724
Yes,

255
00:14:26,747 --> 00:14:30,880
We use paint that won't come off with water once it dries.

256
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:34,703
I'll take my time and paint carefully with a fine brush.

257
00:14:34,726 --> 00:14:36,526
Yes,

258
00:14:36,549 --> 00:14:40,167
Take a deep breath and paint steadily.

259
00:14:40,191 --> 00:14:43,724
I've managed to paint the shape of a goldfish!

260
00:14:43,747 --> 00:14:46,720
That looks really good!

261
00:14:46,744 --> 00:14:50,228
The red color is beautiful.

262
00:14:50,251 --> 00:14:53,701
I'll add some green water plants around it too.

263
00:14:53,725 --> 00:14:57,895
The balance is perfect—it's a fantastic piece!

264
00:14:57,918 --> 00:15:02,552
What should I write on the paper below the wind chime?

265
00:15:02,575 --> 00:15:07,308
You can write your wishes or name on the paper strip.

266
00:15:07,331 --> 00:15:12,064
I'll write my name and 'good health.'

267
00:15:12,087 --> 00:15:15,102
Please use this brush pen to write.

268
00:15:15,125 --> 00:15:17,159
I've finished writing.

269
00:15:17,182 --> 00:15:19,382
I'll tie it with a string.

270
00:15:19,405 --> 00:15:24,899
Let's dry the paint with a hairdryer.

271
00:15:24,923 --> 00:15:28,523
When the wind blows, it makes a lovely 'chirin' sound.

272
00:15:28,546 --> 00:15:33,162
The serrated edges of the glass create that beautiful sound.

273
00:15:33,185 --> 00:15:36,785
It's such a traditional Japanese sound.

274
00:15:36,808 --> 00:15:38,893
It's so soothing.

275
00:15:38,917 --> 00:15:43,487
I'll carefully pack it in a box for you.

276
00:15:43,510 --> 00:15:48,289
Could you wrap it in bubble wrap to prevent it from breaking?

277
00:15:48,313 --> 00:15:50,046
Yes,

278
00:15:50,069 --> 00:15:54,117
I'll wrap it securely in bubble wrap and place it in the box.

279
00:15:54,141 --> 00:15:58,274
I'll put it in my suitcase to take home.

280
00:15:58,297 --> 00:16:03,994
The fee is 2,800 yen, including the trial session.

281
00:16:04,018 --> 00:16:07,751
Can I pay with a credit card?

282
00:16:07,774 --> 00:16:09,343
Yes,

283
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:12,655
You can also use contactless payment.

284
00:16:12,678 --> 00:16:14,971
I'll pay by card.

285
00:16:14,994 --> 00:16:16,794
Thank you very much!

286
00:16:16,817 --> 00:16:22,417
Please cherish and display your one-of-a-kind wind chime.

287
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,940
Scene 6: New Rules and Fees for Climbing Mt. Fuji

288
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:30,107
I’d like to know about the new climbing rules for Mt. Fuji.

289
00:16:30,130 --> 00:16:35,730
New rules have been introduced this year on the Yamanashi side.

290
00:16:35,753 --> 00:16:38,753
I heard there’s a toll fee now.

291
00:16:38,776 --> 00:16:40,509
How much is it?

292
00:16:40,532 --> 00:16:45,365
There’s a 2,000 yen toll fee per person.

293
00:16:45,388 --> 00:16:47,761
2,000 yen, right?

294
00:16:47,785 --> 00:16:51,318
Is that separate from the conservation donation?

295
00:16:51,341 --> 00:16:57,308
Yes, it’s separate from the optional 1,000 yen donation.

296
00:16:57,331 --> 00:17:03,731
So that adds up to 3,000 yen per person. That’s correct.

297
00:17:03,754 --> 00:17:06,721
You can pay on-site or online.

298
00:17:06,744 --> 00:17:10,077
Why is there a toll fee?

299
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:14,700
To prevent overcrowding and ensure safety.

300
00:17:14,723 --> 00:17:18,935
Is there a daily limit on the number of climbers?

301
00:17:18,959 --> 00:17:24,559
Yes, only 4,000 people can climb per day.

302
00:17:24,582 --> 00:17:29,600
4,000 people? I’ll need to book early.

303
00:17:29,623 --> 00:17:34,790
You can make a reservation in advance online.

304
00:17:34,813 --> 00:17:38,687
What do I need to show at the trailhead gate?

305
00:17:38,710 --> 00:17:43,243
Show the QR code from your reservation on your phone.

306
00:17:43,266 --> 00:17:46,400
Can I climb at night?

307
00:17:46,423 --> 00:17:52,989
No, the gate is closed from 4 PM to 3 AM.

308
00:17:53,012 --> 00:17:56,379
This is to prevent overnight ‘bullet climbing,’ right?

309
00:17:56,402 --> 00:18:02,260
Yes, we prohibit dangerous overnight climbs without rest.

310
00:18:02,284 --> 00:18:08,725
What about people who booked mountain huts?

311
00:18:08,748 --> 00:18:12,326
Those with mountain hut reservations can pass through at night.

312
00:18:12,350 --> 00:18:16,083
Booking a mountain hut is really important, then.

313
00:18:16,106 --> 00:18:21,376
The Shizuoka side route now also requires advance registration.

314
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:25,600
I’ll follow the rules and climb safely.

315
00:18:25,623 --> 00:18:30,223
Don’t forget to bring warm clothing and rain gear.

316
00:18:30,245 --> 00:18:34,012
Is it really as cold as winter at the summit, even in summer?

317
00:18:34,035 --> 00:18:39,848
Yes, temperatures at the summit can drop to around 5°C.

318
00:18:39,872 --> 00:18:43,608
I’ll prepare warm clothes and hiking boots.

319
00:18:43,631 --> 00:18:47,165
Bring water and a flashlight too.

320
00:18:47,188 --> 00:18:50,032
We have to take our trash back with us, right?

321
00:18:50,056 --> 00:18:54,889
Yes, you must carry out all your trash.

322
00:18:54,912 --> 00:18:59,128
Thanks for explaining the rules in detail.

323
00:18:59,151 --> 00:19:03,385
Please check the official website for more details.

324
00:19:03,408 --> 00:19:07,343
Okay, I’ll check the booking site today.

325
00:19:07,366 --> 00:19:11,533
Hope the weather is clear so you get a great view!

326
00:19:11,556 --> 00:19:15,822
Yes, I’ll take photos and share them with you!

327
00:19:15,845 --> 00:19:19,179
Make it a wonderful memory!

328
00:19:19,202 --> 00:19:22,008
I’ll prioritize safety and climb carefully.

329
00:19:22,031 --> 00:19:24,698
Take care and have a safe trip!

330
00:19:24,721 --> 00:19:26,221
Scene 7: Guide to Booking Mt. Fuji Online

331
00:19:26,221 --> 00:19:28,188
Excuse me.

332
00:19:28,211 --> 00:19:32,427
Can you explain how to book Mt. Fuji online?

333
00:19:32,450 --> 00:19:34,483
Welcome!

334
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:38,873
You can make a reservation using your computer or smartphone.

335
00:19:38,896 --> 00:19:42,929
Which official website should we visit?

336
00:19:42,952 --> 00:19:47,286
Please visit the official Mount Fuji website.

337
00:19:47,309 --> 00:19:52,358
Can I change the site language to English?

338
00:19:52,381 --> 00:19:54,015
Yes,

339
00:19:54,038 --> 00:19:59,887
You can select English or Chinese at the top right of the screen.

340
00:19:59,910 --> 00:20:02,643
Changed to English.

341
00:20:02,666 --> 00:20:06,399
Which button should I press next?

342
00:20:06,423 --> 00:20:11,195
Please click the red button labeled 'Climbing Reservation'.

343
00:20:11,219 --> 00:20:12,788
Done.

344
00:20:12,812 --> 00:20:16,578
The date selection screen for your climb has appeared.

345
00:20:16,601 --> 00:20:20,368
Please choose the date you'd like to climb.

346
00:20:20,392 --> 00:20:24,638
I'll select Sunday, August 10th.

347
00:20:24,662 --> 00:20:28,062
We'll also choose the trailhead route.

348
00:20:28,085 --> 00:20:30,942
I'll go with the Yoshida Trail.

349
00:20:30,965 --> 00:20:33,575
How many people are in your group?

350
00:20:33,598 --> 00:20:36,034
Two people.

351
00:20:36,058 --> 00:20:39,197
Selecting two people.

352
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:43,186
Do you see the climbing fee and conservation contribution displayed?

353
00:20:43,209 --> 00:20:44,809
Yes,

354
00:20:44,832 --> 00:20:50,166
The climbing fee is 2,000 yen, and the contribution is 1,000 yen.

355
00:20:50,189 --> 00:20:55,662
That's 3,000 yen per person, so 6,000 yen for two.

356
00:20:55,686 --> 00:21:00,355
Can I pay with a credit card?

357
00:21:00,378 --> 00:21:02,111
Yes,

358
00:21:02,134 --> 00:21:06,874
You can enter your card details to complete the payment.

359
00:21:06,897 --> 00:21:11,131
I've entered the card number and expiration date.

360
00:21:11,153 --> 00:21:14,491
Please click the 'Complete Payment' button.

361
00:21:14,514 --> 00:21:16,048
Done.

362
00:21:16,071 --> 00:21:19,873
A QR code appeared on the screen.

363
00:21:19,896 --> 00:21:24,896
Please save that QR code on your smartphone.

364
00:21:24,919 --> 00:21:28,559
I'll save it as a screenshot.

365
00:21:28,583 --> 00:21:33,383
Show this QR code at the trailhead gate on the day of your climb.

366
00:21:33,406 --> 00:21:37,096
Can I show a printed copy instead?

367
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,772
Yes,

368
00:21:38,795 --> 00:21:42,374
Yes, bringing a printed copy is fine too.

369
00:21:42,398 --> 00:21:45,846
I'll print it out and bring it along.

370
00:21:45,869 --> 00:21:48,136
That’ll give you peace of mind.

371
00:21:48,159 --> 00:21:51,092
Did you receive a confirmation email?

372
00:21:51,115 --> 00:21:52,649
Yes,

373
00:21:52,672 --> 00:21:56,638
I got the completion notification in my email.

374
00:21:56,661 --> 00:22:01,301
Your Mount Fuji climb reservation is now complete.

375
00:22:01,325 --> 00:22:05,258
The steps were clear and easy to follow!

376
00:22:05,281 --> 00:22:10,714
If the weather is bad and the climb is canceled, you’ll get a refund.

377
00:22:10,737 --> 00:22:14,337
A refund system is very thoughtful.

378
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:18,960
Don’t forget to prepare your bus tickets to the trailhead too.

379
00:22:18,983 --> 00:22:23,383
I’ll book the express bus from Shinjuku online as well.

380
00:22:23,406 --> 00:22:25,740
Your preparations are perfect!

381
00:22:25,763 --> 00:22:28,529
Please take care and have a safe trip.

382
00:22:28,552 --> 00:22:30,221
Thank you very much!

383
00:22:30,245 --> 00:22:32,211
I’ll enjoy the climb!

384
00:22:32,234 --> 00:22:35,470
Wishing you an amazing climbing experience!

385
00:22:35,494 --> 00:22:36,994
Scene 8: Mountain Climbing Routes and Precautions

386
00:22:36,994 --> 00:22:38,960
Excuse me.

387
00:22:38,983 --> 00:22:42,456
Is this the information center at the 5th station?

388
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:45,751
Yes, this is the place.

389
00:22:45,775 --> 00:22:47,775
Welcome!

390
00:22:47,799 --> 00:22:52,732
Could you tell me about the climbing routes to the summit?

391
00:22:52,755 --> 00:22:56,921
Here’s a map of the Yoshida Trail for you.

392
00:22:56,944 --> 00:22:59,036
Thank you.

393
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:02,993
How long does it take to reach the summit?

394
00:23:03,016 --> 00:23:10,258
It takes about 6 hours to ascend and 3.5 hours to descend.

395
00:23:10,282 --> 00:23:15,482
Is there anything I should be careful about when climbing?

396
00:23:15,505 --> 00:23:22,505
Be careful of altitude sickness. How can I prevent it?

397
00:23:22,528 --> 00:23:27,607
Take it easy and rest for at least an hour at the fifth station.

398
00:23:27,630 --> 00:23:31,312
This helps your body acclimate to the altitude.

399
00:23:31,336 --> 00:23:33,071
Yes, you can!

400
00:23:33,095 --> 00:23:36,528
Make sure to stay hydrated too.

401
00:23:36,551 --> 00:23:40,084
Are there restrooms during the climb?

402
00:23:40,107 --> 00:23:44,541
Each mountain lodge has pay-to-use restrooms.

403
00:23:44,565 --> 00:23:48,610
How much do they cost per use?

404
00:23:48,633 --> 00:23:54,167
You’ll need to leave a tip of 200 to 300 yen per use.

405
00:23:54,190 --> 00:23:57,756
I’ll bring 100-yen coins with me.

406
00:23:57,779 --> 00:24:01,589
Keeping small change in your wallet will come in handy.

407
00:24:01,613 --> 00:24:05,213
Can I buy water along the way?

408
00:24:05,236 --> 00:24:07,036
Yes, you can!

409
00:24:07,059 --> 00:24:12,118
You can buy water and snacks at the mountain lodge shops.

410
00:24:12,141 --> 00:24:15,574
Are prices higher up on the mountain?

411
00:24:15,598 --> 00:24:20,417
A bottle of water can cost around 500 yen.

412
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:22,339
I see.

413
00:24:22,363 --> 00:24:25,696
I’ll buy water at the fifth station before heading up.

414
00:24:25,719 --> 00:24:28,586
That’s a smart decision.

415
00:24:28,609 --> 00:24:32,542
What’s the weather like at the summit today?

416
00:24:32,565 --> 00:24:37,332
Winds will pick up in the afternoon, so be careful.

417
00:24:37,355 --> 00:24:40,488
I’ll wear warm layers for the climb.

418
00:24:40,511 --> 00:24:45,009
Temperatures at the summit can drop to around 5°C.

419
00:24:45,033 --> 00:24:48,999
I’ve got gloves and a warm hat too.

420
00:24:49,022 --> 00:24:51,956
You’re very well-prepared!

421
00:24:51,979 --> 00:24:57,452
What should I do if I start feeling unwell?

422
00:24:57,475 --> 00:25:03,875
Rest at the nearest mountain lodge right away. Don’t push yourself.

423
00:25:03,898 --> 00:25:08,876
The guide map has emergency contact numbers listed.

424
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:12,595
I’ll keep the guide map in my pocket.

425
00:25:12,618 --> 00:25:15,818
Please prioritize safety during your climb.

426
00:25:15,841 --> 00:25:19,336
I’ve got a headlamp packed in my backpack.

427
00:25:19,359 --> 00:25:23,458
It’s best to reach the lodge before dark.

428
00:25:23,482 --> 00:25:27,016
Thank you for the detailed advice.

429
00:25:27,039 --> 00:25:31,309
Enjoy the breathtaking views up there!

430
00:25:31,332 --> 00:25:33,765
I’ll be careful on my way.

431
00:25:33,788 --> 00:25:36,421
Take care and have a safe climb!

432
00:25:36,444 --> 00:25:37,944
Scene 9: Check-in at a Mountain Lodge

433
00:25:37,944 --> 00:25:42,178
Excuse me, I’d like to check in.

434
00:25:42,201 --> 00:25:44,034
Welcome!

435
00:25:44,057 --> 00:25:48,156
Welcome to the mountain lodge at the eighth station!

436
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:50,654
I’m Maria, the one who made the reservation.

437
00:25:50,678 --> 00:25:53,011
Maria, correct?

438
00:25:53,034 --> 00:25:56,074
I’ve confirmed your name.

439
00:25:56,097 --> 00:25:59,236
I booked for two people.

440
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:03,593
We’ve prepared a room for the two of you.

441
00:26:03,616 --> 00:26:06,554
Where will we be sleeping?

442
00:26:06,578 --> 00:26:11,944
Please use sleeping bags number 12 and 13 on the second floor.

443
00:26:11,967 --> 00:26:16,401
The sleeping bags are lined up here.

444
00:26:16,424 --> 00:26:20,197
It’s a shared room with other guests.

445
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:23,420
Where should I put my luggage?

446
00:26:23,443 --> 00:26:27,677
Please place your backpack on the shelf above your head.

447
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:29,666
Understood.

448
00:26:29,689 --> 00:26:31,705
I’ll put it on the shelf.

449
00:26:31,729 --> 00:26:34,867
Dinner is ready!

450
00:26:34,890 --> 00:26:37,857
What time is dinner served until?

451
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:43,769
Dinner is available in the dining hall from 6:00 PM to 7:00 PM.

452
00:26:43,793 --> 00:26:47,026
What’s on the dinner menu?

453
00:26:47,049 --> 00:26:52,016
We’ll be serving warm curry rice and hot tea.

454
00:26:52,039 --> 00:26:57,015
I’m glad we’re having warm curry rice—it’s freezing up here!

455
00:26:57,038 --> 00:27:02,081
The mountain gets really cold, so make sure to eat plenty.

456
00:27:02,105 --> 00:27:05,438
I’ll head to the dining hall to eat.

457
00:27:05,461 --> 00:27:09,307
The dining hall is just down the hall this way.

458
00:27:09,330 --> 00:27:13,812
Can I get a breakfast boxed lunch too?

459
00:27:13,835 --> 00:27:17,914
We’ll provide the boxed lunch when you come for dinner.

460
00:27:17,938 --> 00:27:22,738
I’ll eat it at the summit tomorrow morning.

461
00:27:22,761 --> 00:27:26,728
What time do we leave for the summit tomorrow?

462
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:30,566
We’d like to depart at 2:00 AM.

463
00:27:30,590 --> 00:27:35,323
The trail gets extremely crowded around 2:00 AM.

464
00:27:35,346 --> 00:27:38,948
Should we leave earlier?

465
00:27:38,972 --> 00:27:40,538
Yes, you can!

466
00:27:40,561 --> 00:27:44,833
I recommend leaving at 1:30 AM instead.

467
00:27:44,856 --> 00:27:48,790
Got it—we’ll leave at 1:30 AM.

468
00:27:48,813 --> 00:27:54,213
Lights-out is at 9:00 PM.

469
00:27:54,236 --> 00:27:58,304
The lights go out at 9:00 PM, right?

470
00:27:58,327 --> 00:27:59,415
Yes, you can!

471
00:27:59,439 --> 00:28:03,572
Please rest quietly after 9:00 PM.

472
00:28:03,595 --> 00:28:07,195
I’ll prepare my headlamp.

473
00:28:07,218 --> 00:28:13,051
Keep the light dim so it doesn’t bother others.

474
00:28:13,074 --> 00:28:16,108
I’ll get ready quietly and carefully.

475
00:28:16,131 --> 00:28:19,799
You can buy water and tea at the shop.

476
00:28:19,822 --> 00:28:23,588
I’d like to buy a bottle of water.

477
00:28:23,611 --> 00:28:28,178
A bottle of water costs 500 yen.

478
00:28:28,201 --> 00:28:30,288
Here’s 500 yen.

479
00:28:30,312 --> 00:28:31,964
Thank you.

480
00:28:31,987 --> 00:28:36,353
Get some rest and prepare for tomorrow’s climb.

481
00:28:36,376 --> 00:28:37,876
Scene 10: Renting Gear for Climbing Mt. Fuji

482
00:28:37,876 --> 00:28:39,876
Excuse me.

483
00:28:39,899 --> 00:28:43,833
I’d like to rent gear for climbing Mt. Fuji.

484
00:28:43,856 --> 00:28:45,624
Welcome!

485
00:28:45,647 --> 00:28:50,014
Welcome to the mountain gear rental shop!

486
00:28:50,037 --> 00:28:54,332
Can I rent cold-weather gear and a headlamp?

487
00:28:54,355 --> 00:28:55,975
Yes,

488
00:28:55,998 --> 00:29:00,598
You can rent them as a set in this section.

489
00:29:00,621 --> 00:29:03,863
Can I try on the sizes?

490
00:29:03,887 --> 00:29:08,854
We have a fitting room—go ahead and check the fit.

491
00:29:08,877 --> 00:29:12,296
I’ll try on the M-sized jacket.

492
00:29:12,319 --> 00:29:14,124
How does it feel?

493
00:29:14,147 --> 00:29:16,442
Does it fit well?

494
00:29:16,466 --> 00:29:19,139
It fits perfectly!

495
00:29:19,162 --> 00:29:22,730
Does it have windproof and waterproof features?

496
00:29:22,754 --> 00:29:24,354
Yes,

497
00:29:24,377 --> 00:29:29,577
It’s made of high-quality material that blocks strong winds and heavy rain.

498
00:29:29,600 --> 00:29:32,867
Are the pants included in the set?

499
00:29:32,890 --> 00:29:34,424
Yes,

500
00:29:34,447 --> 00:29:39,213
Yes, it’s a full set with a jacket and insulated pants.

501
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:43,636
It’ll be freezing at the summit like winter—this is reassuring!

502
00:29:43,659 --> 00:29:47,509
Next, I’ll give you the headlamp.

503
00:29:47,533 --> 00:29:51,666
Could you show me how to use the headlamp?

504
00:29:51,689 --> 00:29:56,022
Press the top button to turn it on.

505
00:29:56,045 --> 00:29:59,120
Can I adjust the brightness?

506
00:29:59,143 --> 00:30:04,511
Press the button twice for a brighter light.

507
00:30:04,535 --> 00:30:07,735
Are the batteries new?

508
00:30:07,758 --> 00:30:09,291
Yes,

509
00:30:09,314 --> 00:30:13,530
We've installed new AA batteries for you.

510
00:30:13,553 --> 00:30:16,886
Can I also get some spare batteries?

511
00:30:16,909 --> 00:30:21,843
You can add spare batteries for just an extra 200 yen.

512
00:30:21,866 --> 00:30:25,041
I'll take the spare batteries as well, please.

513
00:30:25,064 --> 00:30:30,763
Adjust the rubber strap of the headlamp to fit your head size.

514
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:32,920
I've tightened the strap.

515
00:30:32,943 --> 00:30:35,276
It fits perfectly now.

516
00:30:35,299 --> 00:30:39,699
Would you like to rent some mountaineering gaiters or spats as well?

517
00:30:39,722 --> 00:30:43,295
Those are covers to keep sand out, right?

518
00:30:43,319 --> 00:30:45,754
I'd like to rent those too.

519
00:30:45,777 --> 00:30:50,196
They protect your feet, so I'll add them to your set.

520
00:30:50,219 --> 00:30:52,986
Where should I return these items?

521
00:30:53,009 --> 00:30:57,342
You can return them to the collection box at the Fifth Station.

522
00:30:57,365 --> 00:31:02,499
It's so convenient that I can return them at the Fifth Station!

523
00:31:02,522 --> 00:31:07,000
You can return them in the box even if they're muddy.

524
00:31:07,024 --> 00:31:10,065
That's great—I don’t have to wash them!

525
00:31:10,088 --> 00:31:14,661
Let me calculate the rental fee for your 3-day, 2-night trip.

526
00:31:14,685 --> 00:31:17,168
How much will it be in total?

527
00:31:17,191 --> 00:31:22,673
The total comes to 6,800 yen, including the set fee and insurance.

528
00:31:22,696 --> 00:31:25,463
I'll pay with a credit card.

529
00:31:25,486 --> 00:31:29,653
Yes, you can pay with a simple tap.

530
00:31:29,676 --> 00:31:31,957
Payment completed.

531
00:31:31,980 --> 00:31:35,180
You’ve packed everything into a large bag for me—thanks!

532
00:31:35,203 --> 00:31:39,222
You can even send this bag directly to the Fifth Station.

533
00:31:39,245 --> 00:31:43,457
We’ll load it onto the express bus, so no worries.

534
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:47,251
Wishing you a safe and amazing climbing experience!

535
00:31:47,274 --> 00:31:48,774
Scene 11: The Convenience of Contactless Payments

536
00:31:48,774 --> 00:31:52,389
Did you watch the news this morning?

537
00:31:52,413 --> 00:31:55,614
No, I didn’t.

538
00:31:55,638 --> 00:31:57,839
What was the news about?

539
00:31:57,862 --> 00:32:03,628
It was about how contactless payments are increasing in Japanese stores.

540
00:32:03,651 --> 00:32:06,296
Contactless payments?

541
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:10,694
You just tap your card or phone to pay.

542
00:32:10,718 --> 00:32:12,285
Yes,

543
00:32:12,308 --> 00:32:18,241
It lets you shop quickly without fumbling for change.

544
00:32:18,264 --> 00:32:24,633
That’s incredibly convenient for foreign travelers too!

545
00:32:24,657 --> 00:32:29,457
Can I use contactless payments with my credit card?

546
00:32:29,479 --> 00:32:31,218
Yes,

547
00:32:31,242 --> 00:32:36,691
Yes, you can use contactless payments with international brand cards.

548
00:32:36,714 --> 00:32:42,603
Can I also use Apple Pay or Google Pay on my phone?

549
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:44,124
Yes,

550
00:32:44,148 --> 00:32:48,714
Just tap your phone on the terminal to pay.

551
00:32:48,737 --> 00:32:54,737
Do I need to enter a PIN at the register?

552
00:32:54,760 --> 00:33:00,394
For purchases under a certain amount, you don’t need a signature or PIN.

553
00:33:00,417 --> 00:33:04,435
That makes payments so much faster!

554
00:33:04,459 --> 00:33:09,952
It reduces checkout lines and makes shopping stress-free.

555
00:33:09,975 --> 00:33:14,375
Is tax-free processing also becoming more digital?

556
00:33:14,398 --> 00:33:16,134
Yes,

557
00:33:16,158 --> 00:33:20,891
Just scan your passport with the machine—it’s that easy!

558
00:33:20,914 --> 00:33:26,988
More stores are switching to digital receipts instead of paper.

559
00:33:27,012 --> 00:33:32,212
You can receive receipts via email or an app.

560
00:33:32,235 --> 00:33:37,045
No more paper receipts cluttering up your wallet!

561
00:33:37,068 --> 00:33:41,201
It’s an eco-friendly system too—great for the environment!

562
00:33:41,224 --> 00:33:45,200
Can I use contactless payments at convenience stores and department stores?

563
00:33:45,224 --> 00:33:47,024
Yes,

564
00:33:47,047 --> 00:33:50,523
Most chain stores support it.

565
00:33:50,547 --> 00:33:55,914
Are contactless payments becoming more common in rural tourist areas too?

566
00:33:55,937 --> 00:33:57,670
Yes,

567
00:33:57,693 --> 00:34:02,326
Touch payments are becoming more common on buses and trains, too.

568
00:34:02,349 --> 00:34:07,349
You can pass through the ticket gate without buying a ticket.

569
00:34:07,372 --> 00:34:12,306
Just use your regular credit card to ride.

570
00:34:12,329 --> 00:34:17,974
Shopping and getting around in Japan is so much easier now!

571
00:34:17,997 --> 00:34:19,564
Yes,

572
00:34:19,587 --> 00:34:23,059
No need to worry about preparing cash.

573
00:34:23,082 --> 00:34:27,849
I’m happy I don’t have to deal with counting coins anymore.

574
00:34:27,872 --> 00:34:34,328
Many terminals now support English and multiple languages.

575
00:34:34,352 --> 00:34:39,885
Even if you don’t speak the same language as the staff, you can operate the screen.

576
00:34:39,908 --> 00:34:45,400
You can enjoy sightseeing stress-free and with peace of mind.

577
00:34:45,423 --> 00:34:49,557
We’ll use touch payment at today’s store, too.

578
00:34:49,580 --> 00:34:54,413
Hold your card over the reader until you hear a beep.

579
00:34:54,436 --> 00:34:58,312
Thank you for showing me how to do it.

580
00:34:58,336 --> 00:35:02,336
Enjoy a smooth and comfortable shopping experience!

581
00:35:02,359 --> 00:35:07,202
I’ll check if my card is compatible.

582
00:35:07,225 --> 00:35:11,859
If your card has a wave symbol, you’re good to go!

583
00:35:11,883 --> 00:35:15,516
Oh, it has the wave symbol!

584
00:35:15,539 --> 00:35:19,838
Then you can use touch payment!

585
00:35:19,862 --> 00:35:23,795
I’ll go ahead and use my card for shopping.

586
00:35:23,818 --> 00:35:25,318
Scene 12: Shopping Conversations / Basic Shopping Dialogues

587
00:35:25,318 --> 00:35:29,005
Excuse me, I’ll take this, please.

588
00:35:29,029 --> 00:35:31,196
Welcome!

589
00:35:31,219 --> 00:35:34,352
You’ve got a bento and tea, right?

590
00:35:34,375 --> 00:35:38,342
Yes, a bento and tea.

591
00:35:38,365 --> 00:35:42,532
Would you like me to heat the bento in the microwave?

592
00:35:42,555 --> 00:35:45,927
Yes, please warm it up.

593
00:35:45,951 --> 00:35:48,084
Understood.

594
00:35:48,107 --> 00:35:52,947
I’ll heat it at 500 watts for 40 seconds.

595
00:35:52,971 --> 00:35:54,646
That’s very helpful.

596
00:35:54,669 --> 00:35:58,204
I’d like to eat it warm.

597
00:35:58,227 --> 00:36:03,260
Would you like a plastic bag?

598
00:36:03,283 --> 00:36:09,217
No, thank you. I have my own reusable bag.

599
00:36:09,240 --> 00:36:11,107
Understood.

600
00:36:11,130 --> 00:36:14,463
I’ll put it in your reusable bag.

601
00:36:14,486 --> 00:36:16,020
Thank you.

602
00:36:16,043 --> 00:36:19,136
Could I also get a pair of chopsticks?

603
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:24,566
Sure, I’ll include chopsticks and a napkin.

604
00:36:24,589 --> 00:36:27,234
Could I also get a spoon, please?

605
00:36:27,258 --> 00:36:30,791
Of course, I’ll add a spoon as well.

606
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:34,500
How much is the total?

607
00:36:34,523 --> 00:36:38,982
The total comes to 780 yen.

608
00:36:39,006 --> 00:36:43,373
Can I pay with touch payment using my credit card?

609
00:36:43,396 --> 00:36:49,362
Yes, you can use touch payment with your credit card.

610
00:36:49,385 --> 00:36:53,359
Can I also use Apple Pay on my phone?

611
00:36:53,383 --> 00:36:58,316
Yes, you can use Apple Pay as well.

612
00:36:58,339 --> 00:37:01,116
I'll pay with a credit card.

613
00:37:01,139 --> 00:37:03,273
Do I press the screen?

614
00:37:03,297 --> 00:37:09,335
Please tap the credit card button on the screen.

615
00:37:09,359 --> 00:37:10,959
Tapped it.

616
00:37:10,982 --> 00:37:14,116
Where do I hold my card?

617
00:37:14,139 --> 00:37:19,172
Place your card over the terminal where the light is blue.

618
00:37:19,195 --> 00:37:22,462
I’ll place my card here.

619
00:37:22,485 --> 00:37:26,779
Keep it there until you hear a beep.

620
00:37:26,803 --> 00:37:29,736
It beeped!

621
00:37:29,759 --> 00:37:32,294
Payment complete!

622
00:37:32,318 --> 00:37:34,851
Please take your card.

623
00:37:34,874 --> 00:37:38,647
No signature or PIN required?

624
00:37:38,671 --> 00:37:45,076
That's right, since it's a small amount, no signature or PIN is needed.

625
00:37:45,099 --> 00:37:47,974
It's so fast and convenient!

626
00:37:47,997 --> 00:37:50,997
Here's your receipt.

627
00:37:51,020 --> 00:37:54,654
Can I get an e-receipt instead?

628
00:37:54,677 --> 00:37:59,810
Sure, please scan the QR code on the screen with your smartphone.

629
00:37:59,833 --> 00:38:02,067
Scanned it.

630
00:38:02,090 --> 00:38:05,690
Your receipt has been sent to your phone.

631
00:38:05,713 --> 00:38:10,079
So I can save it without printing a paper receipt.

632
00:38:10,102 --> 00:38:14,950
Yes, it helps keep my wallet nice and organized.

633
00:38:14,973 --> 00:38:18,973
I'll bring your warm bento right away.

634
00:38:18,996 --> 00:38:22,483
Thank you for your kind assistance.

635
00:38:22,507 --> 00:38:23,940
Thank you.

636
00:38:23,963 --> 00:38:27,330
We look forward to your next visit.

637
00:38:27,353 --> 00:38:28,853
Scene 13: How to Use a Self-Checkout Machine

638
00:38:28,853 --> 00:38:30,820
Excuse me.

639
00:38:30,843 --> 00:38:34,454
Could you show me how to use the self-checkout?

640
00:38:34,477 --> 00:38:35,811
Yes, you can!

641
00:38:35,834 --> 00:38:38,000
I'd be happy to help.

642
00:38:38,023 --> 00:38:41,223
Please touch the screen to begin.

643
00:38:41,246 --> 00:38:46,330
Can I change the language to English?

644
00:38:46,354 --> 00:38:47,989
Yes, you can!

645
00:38:48,013 --> 00:38:52,746
Press the 'English' button in the top right corner.

646
00:38:52,769 --> 00:38:55,659
The screen is now in English.

647
00:38:55,683 --> 00:38:58,616
What's next?

648
00:38:58,639 --> 00:39:03,850
Hold the product's barcode up to the red scanner.

649
00:39:03,873 --> 00:39:08,770
Let me scan the barcode on this snack.

650
00:39:08,793 --> 00:39:11,881
It beeped!

651
00:39:11,904 --> 00:39:14,704
The product name appeared on the screen.

652
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:18,961
This apple doesn’t have a barcode.

653
00:39:18,984 --> 00:39:24,855
Press the 'No Barcode' button on the screen.

654
00:39:24,878 --> 00:39:30,478
Select 'Apple' from the fruit icons.

655
00:39:30,501 --> 00:39:31,951
Yes, you can!

656
00:39:31,975 --> 00:39:35,775
Choose one apple and touch the screen.

657
00:39:35,798 --> 00:39:39,365
It's been registered.

658
00:39:39,388 --> 00:39:44,721
What about this meat with a 20% off sticker?

659
00:39:44,744 --> 00:39:49,678
Just scan the barcode on the discount sticker.

660
00:39:49,701 --> 00:39:54,837
It beeped, and the price updated to 20% off!

661
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:58,860
It scanned correctly.

662
00:39:58,883 --> 00:40:02,662
I'd like to buy one plastic bag.

663
00:40:02,686 --> 00:40:09,252
Press 'Need a Bag' on the screen and select one.

664
00:40:09,275 --> 00:40:12,523
I selected one.

665
00:40:12,547 --> 00:40:15,422
Where are the bags?

666
00:40:15,446 --> 00:40:21,112
The 5-yen paid bags are next to the register.

667
00:40:21,135 --> 00:40:25,582
Where should I place my reusable bag if I have one?

668
00:40:25,605 --> 00:40:31,205
Place your reusable bag on the weighing scale to the left.

669
00:40:31,228 --> 00:40:35,869
The weight sensor is checking the weight.

670
00:40:35,893 --> 00:40:41,260
Please place scanned items directly into the bag.

671
00:40:41,283 --> 00:40:44,735
An alarm beeped!

672
00:40:44,759 --> 00:40:46,364
Why did that happen?

673
00:40:46,387 --> 00:40:50,753
Because you moved the bag before placing the item inside.

674
00:40:50,776 --> 00:40:53,344
Let me clear that.

675
00:40:53,368 --> 00:40:54,935
Thank you.

676
00:40:54,958 --> 00:40:57,253
The error is gone.

677
00:40:57,276 --> 00:41:00,209
Proceeding to payment.

678
00:41:00,232 --> 00:41:02,999
Please proceed with the payment.

679
00:41:03,022 --> 00:41:05,856
Select your payment method.

680
00:41:05,879 --> 00:41:09,113
Can I use contactless payment?

681
00:41:09,136 --> 00:41:14,029
Yes, you can use touch payment with your credit card.

682
00:41:14,052 --> 00:41:18,585
Press the credit card button.

683
00:41:18,608 --> 00:41:23,085
Tap your card on the illuminated card terminal on the right.

684
00:41:23,108 --> 00:41:27,382
Hold it there until you hear a beep.

685
00:41:27,406 --> 00:41:29,739
Your payment is complete.

686
00:41:29,762 --> 00:41:32,129
Please take your card.

687
00:41:32,152 --> 00:41:35,201
Here’s your receipt and proof of purchase.

688
00:41:35,225 --> 00:41:40,591
Keep your receipt—it’s needed for returns.

689
00:41:40,614 --> 00:41:42,348
Understood.

690
00:41:42,371 --> 00:41:44,773
I’ll put it in my wallet.

691
00:41:44,797 --> 00:41:48,963
Great job using the self-checkout!

692
00:41:48,986 --> 00:41:53,820
The English instructions made it so easy to use.

693
00:41:53,843 --> 00:41:55,327
Thank you.

694
00:41:55,350 --> 00:41:57,684
We look forward to your next visit!

695
00:41:57,707 --> 00:41:59,207
Scene 14: How to Use Digital Receipts

696
00:41:59,207 --> 00:42:01,042
Excuse me.

697
00:42:01,065 --> 00:42:04,832
I’d like to check out these clothes and this bag.

698
00:42:04,855 --> 00:42:06,551
Welcome!

699
00:42:06,574 --> 00:42:08,413
Thank you.

700
00:42:08,436 --> 00:42:12,318
Can I get a digital receipt?

701
00:42:12,342 --> 00:42:13,708
Yes, you can!

702
00:42:13,731 --> 00:42:18,398
We can issue a paperless digital receipt.

703
00:42:18,421 --> 00:42:21,788
So, no paper receipts—just digital?

704
00:42:21,811 --> 00:42:23,344
Yes, you can!

705
00:42:23,367 --> 00:42:27,434
We’ll send the receipt data directly to your phone.

706
00:42:27,457 --> 00:42:30,099
How do I receive it?

707
00:42:30,123 --> 00:42:35,123
Scan the QR code on the register screen with your phone.

708
00:42:35,146 --> 00:42:37,635
I’ll scan it with my camera.

709
00:42:37,658 --> 00:42:40,392
Got it—scanned successfully!

710
00:42:40,415 --> 00:42:42,900
Did the screen open?

711
00:42:42,924 --> 00:42:43,990
Yes, you can!

712
00:42:44,013 --> 00:42:47,660
I see a screen to enter my email address.

713
00:42:47,684 --> 00:42:51,250
Please enter your email address.

714
00:42:51,273 --> 00:42:54,206
I’ve entered my email address.

715
00:42:54,229 --> 00:42:56,763
Press the send button.

716
00:42:56,786 --> 00:42:58,186
Yes, you can!

717
00:42:58,209 --> 00:43:00,475
The digital receipt has been sent!

718
00:43:00,498 --> 00:43:04,032
I received the digital receipt on my phone.

719
00:43:04,055 --> 00:43:05,621
I’ve confirmed it.

720
00:43:05,644 --> 00:43:07,411
Thank you.

721
00:43:07,434 --> 00:43:10,246
It was sent correctly.

722
00:43:10,270 --> 00:43:14,109
This is so convenient—no more paper cluttering my wallet!

723
00:43:14,132 --> 00:43:19,500
It’s eco-friendly and very popular with customers.

724
00:43:19,524 --> 00:43:24,421
Can I use this digital receipt for tax-free procedures?

725
00:43:24,444 --> 00:43:25,778
Yes, you can!

726
00:43:25,801 --> 00:43:30,138
Yes, you can use the digital receipt for tax-free processing.

727
00:43:30,161 --> 00:43:33,295
I’d like to use it at the tax-free counter.

728
00:43:33,318 --> 00:43:37,813
Please show the screen on your phone at the tax-free counter on the 5th floor.

729
00:43:37,836 --> 00:43:41,236
Do I just show the screen on my phone?

730
00:43:41,259 --> 00:43:42,676
Yes, you can!

731
00:43:42,700 --> 00:43:46,194
The staff will scan the barcode on your screen.

732
00:43:46,217 --> 00:43:50,296
It works just like a paper receipt, right?

733
00:43:50,320 --> 00:43:51,720
Yes, you can!

734
00:43:51,743 --> 00:43:55,759
Exactly the same—no need to worry!

735
00:43:55,782 --> 00:43:59,439
Can I use it for returns or exchanges too?

736
00:43:59,463 --> 00:44:04,033
For returns, just show your digital receipt.

737
00:44:04,057 --> 00:44:07,940
I love not having to worry about losing receipts!

738
00:44:07,963 --> 00:44:12,096
Your total comes to 12,000 yen.

739
00:44:12,119 --> 00:44:15,653
I’ll pay with contactless credit card.

740
00:44:15,676 --> 00:44:18,171
Please tap your card on the terminal.

741
00:44:18,195 --> 00:44:19,828
Tapped it.

742
00:44:19,852 --> 00:44:22,852
It made a *ping* sound!

743
00:44:22,875 --> 00:44:25,154
Payment complete!

744
00:44:25,178 --> 00:44:29,945
Your digital receipt and payment details are all set.

745
00:44:29,968 --> 00:44:33,935
Let me neatly bag your items for you.

746
00:44:33,958 --> 00:44:37,094
Thank you so much for the careful packaging!

747
00:44:37,117 --> 00:44:41,084
Please proceed to the duty-free counter on the fifth floor as well.

748
00:44:41,107 --> 00:44:42,445
Got it.

749
00:44:42,468 --> 00:44:44,468
I'll take the elevator.

750
00:44:44,491 --> 00:44:46,291
Thank you very much!

751
00:44:46,314 --> 00:44:49,248
Enjoy your shopping!

752
00:44:49,271 --> 00:44:50,771
Scene 15: How to Use QR Code Ordering

753
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:52,642
Excuse me.

754
00:44:52,666 --> 00:44:54,506
Table for two, please.

755
00:44:54,529 --> 00:44:56,611
Would you like to be seated?

756
00:44:56,635 --> 00:44:58,681
Welcome!

757
00:44:58,705 --> 00:45:02,271
Right this way to your table.

758
00:45:02,294 --> 00:45:03,987
Thank you.

759
00:45:04,011 --> 00:45:07,744
Could we get a menu, please?

760
00:45:07,767 --> 00:45:13,701
Our restaurant uses a QR code ordering system at each table.

761
00:45:13,724 --> 00:45:17,000
QR code ordering, right?

762
00:45:17,023 --> 00:45:20,757
Will you be using your own smartphone?

763
00:45:20,780 --> 00:45:22,277
Yes, you can!

764
00:45:22,300 --> 00:45:27,342
Please scan the QR code on this stand with your camera.

765
00:45:27,365 --> 00:45:29,899
I scanned it with my camera.

766
00:45:29,922 --> 00:45:33,322
The menu popped up!

767
00:45:33,345 --> 00:45:39,415
You can change the language to English in the top right corner of the screen.

768
00:45:39,438 --> 00:45:42,006
It's in English now.

769
00:45:42,030 --> 00:45:46,502
The photos make it really easy to understand.

770
00:45:46,526 --> 00:45:51,492
Just select the dishes you'd like and add them to your cart.

771
00:45:51,515 --> 00:45:57,849
I'll go with the tonkotsu ramen and the tempura platter.

772
00:45:57,872 --> 00:46:02,353
You can even choose the firmness of your ramen noodles.

773
00:46:02,377 --> 00:46:05,210
I'll take them firm.

774
00:46:05,233 --> 00:46:09,906
I'll add a braised egg as a topping.

775
00:46:09,930 --> 00:46:14,869
Review your cart and press the 'Confirm Order' button.

776
00:46:14,893 --> 00:46:18,227
I pressed the 'Confirm Order' button.

777
00:46:18,250 --> 00:46:19,784
Yes, you can!

778
00:46:19,807 --> 00:46:22,973
Your order has been sent to the kitchen.

779
00:46:22,996 --> 00:46:30,363
That was so easy to order without a paper menu!

780
00:46:30,386 --> 00:46:33,319
Here's your water and a hot towel.

781
00:46:33,342 --> 00:46:34,876
Thank you.

782
00:46:34,899 --> 00:46:39,365
Would you like to order more water from your phone?

783
00:46:39,388 --> 00:46:40,878
Yes, you can!

784
00:46:40,902 --> 00:46:46,635
You can order refills of water for free from your cart.

785
00:46:46,658 --> 00:46:51,592
It's so convenient to order free water refills!

786
00:46:51,615 --> 00:46:53,860
Here you are.

787
00:46:53,883 --> 00:46:57,083
Your tonkotsu ramen and tempura platter.

788
00:46:57,106 --> 00:47:00,559
This ramen looks absolutely beautiful!

789
00:47:00,583 --> 00:47:02,184
Let's dig in!

790
00:47:02,208 --> 00:47:05,741
Please enjoy your meal.

791
00:47:05,764 --> 00:47:10,698
The ramen broth is so rich and delicious!

792
00:47:10,721 --> 00:47:12,287
Thank you.

793
00:47:12,310 --> 00:47:15,344
Would you like to order anything else?

794
00:47:15,368 --> 00:47:20,368
I'll order one matcha ice cream for dessert.

795
00:47:20,391 --> 00:47:25,057
Please order your dessert from the smartphone screen.

796
00:47:25,080 --> 00:47:28,814
I just ordered the matcha ice cream.

797
00:47:28,837 --> 00:47:31,970
Here's your matcha ice cream.

798
00:47:31,993 --> 00:47:34,404
Please enjoy.

799
00:47:34,428 --> 00:47:36,161
That was delicious!

800
00:47:36,184 --> 00:47:38,674
Thank you for the meal.

801
00:47:38,698 --> 00:47:42,710
I'll proceed with your bill.

802
00:47:42,734 --> 00:47:46,867
Can I pay the bill with my smartphone too?

803
00:47:46,890 --> 00:47:48,367
Yes, you can!

804
00:47:48,391 --> 00:47:53,631
Press 'Check Out' on the screen, and you can pay with PayPay.

805
00:47:53,654 --> 00:47:58,654
I'll just scan my PayPay barcode to pay.

806
00:47:58,677 --> 00:48:02,810
Hold your smartphone screen up to the register's scanner.

807
00:48:02,833 --> 00:48:07,600
You’ll likely hear a beep, and your payment will be complete.

808
00:48:07,623 --> 00:48:10,189
We’ve confirmed your payment.

809
00:48:10,212 --> 00:48:11,779
Thank you.

810
00:48:11,802 --> 00:48:16,275
Being able to pay right at the table was so convenient!

811
00:48:16,298 --> 00:48:20,544
If you need a receipt, we’ll provide one at the register.

812
00:48:20,567 --> 00:48:23,025
I’ll take a receipt.

813
00:48:23,049 --> 00:48:24,941
Thank you very much!

814
00:48:24,965 --> 00:48:26,498
Thank you very much!

815
00:48:26,521 --> 00:48:29,091
We look forward to your next visit!

816
00:48:29,115 --> 00:48:30,615
Scene 16: More Immigration Staff to Cut Wait Times

817
00:48:30,615 --> 00:48:34,348
Did you watch the morning news?

818
00:48:34,371 --> 00:48:37,177
No, I didn’t.

819
00:48:37,200 --> 00:48:39,485
What news?

820
00:48:39,508 --> 00:48:44,516
It’s about the Immigration Services Agency.

821
00:48:44,539 --> 00:48:47,106
Oh, immigration news?

822
00:48:47,129 --> 00:48:49,495
What’s it about?

823
00:48:49,518 --> 00:48:55,285
They’re adding over 220 more staff to the counters.

824
00:48:55,308 --> 00:48:58,441
They’re increasing staff?

825
00:48:58,464 --> 00:49:01,546
That should ease the crowds.

826
00:49:01,570 --> 00:49:05,849
Well, the number of foreigners living in Japan has grown.

827
00:49:05,873 --> 00:49:12,345
Shinagawa’s immigration office is always so packed.

828
00:49:12,368 --> 00:49:17,218
Yeah, sometimes you have to wait for hours—it’s tough.

829
00:49:17,241 --> 00:49:22,174
More staff means shorter wait times!

830
00:49:22,197 --> 00:49:26,371
They’re also adding more multilingual staff.

831
00:49:26,395 --> 00:49:30,828
Can I get help in English or Chinese?

832
00:49:30,851 --> 00:49:38,018
Yes, you can consult in English, Chinese, or Vietnamese.

833
00:49:38,041 --> 00:49:43,613
That’s reassuring for foreigners who aren’t confident in Japanese.

834
00:49:43,636 --> 00:49:48,912
Residence status renewals will go more smoothly too.

835
00:49:48,936 --> 00:49:53,308
Can I apply online too?

836
00:49:53,331 --> 00:49:58,465
Yes, they’re also improving online application guidance.

837
00:49:58,488 --> 00:50:03,454
It’ll be a big help if I can handle things without going to the office.

838
00:50:03,477 --> 00:50:08,316
A new phone reservation system is being introduced too.

839
00:50:08,340 --> 00:50:12,815
So I can book by phone or online before going?

840
00:50:12,838 --> 00:50:17,438
Exactly—no more wasted waiting time.

841
00:50:17,461 --> 00:50:22,904
Can I ask about changing my residence card or address too?

842
00:50:22,928 --> 00:50:28,397
Yes, you can consult at the information center.

843
00:50:28,420 --> 00:50:31,066
Is the consultation free?

844
00:50:31,090 --> 00:50:36,363
Yes, they’ll help you kindly and for free.

845
00:50:36,386 --> 00:50:40,820
I have to renew my residence card next month.

846
00:50:40,843 --> 00:50:45,609
You should book and use the new system!

847
00:50:45,632 --> 00:50:49,199
I’ll prepare my documents online.

848
00:50:49,222 --> 00:50:54,555
If you have any questions, just call the helpdesk.

849
00:50:54,578 --> 00:50:58,272
Could you give me the number for English phone support?

850
00:50:58,296 --> 00:51:02,429
You can find it on the official website.

851
00:51:02,452 --> 00:51:05,819
I’ll check the site tonight.

852
00:51:05,842 --> 00:51:11,208
Let’s follow the correct procedures and live in Japan with peace of mind.

853
00:51:11,231 --> 00:51:15,512
Thanks for sharing such detailed news!

854
00:51:15,536 --> 00:51:18,770
I’m glad it was helpful!

855
00:51:18,793 --> 00:51:23,759
I’ll do my best to get my renewal done smoothly!

856
00:51:23,782 --> 00:51:26,316
I’m rooting for you!

857
00:51:26,339 --> 00:51:28,195
Thank you.

858
00:51:28,219 --> 00:51:32,619
I’ll let you know if there’s any more news.

859
00:51:32,642 --> 00:51:35,218
Sounds good, thanks!

860
00:51:35,241 --> 00:51:36,741
Scene 17: Residence Card Renewal Procedure

861
00:51:36,741 --> 00:51:38,608
Excuse me.

862
00:51:38,631 --> 00:51:42,598
I’d like to renew my residence card.

863
00:51:42,621 --> 00:51:44,315
Welcome!

864
00:51:44,338 --> 00:51:47,623
Please proceed to the B counter reception.

865
00:51:47,647 --> 00:51:51,886
Do I need to get a numbered ticket from the ticket machine?

866
00:51:51,910 --> 00:51:53,243
Yes, you can!

867
00:51:53,266 --> 00:51:57,700
Press the blue button to take your numbered ticket.

868
00:51:57,723 --> 00:52:00,338
I’ve taken my numbered ticket.

869
00:52:00,361 --> 00:52:03,561
It says B-15.

870
00:52:03,585 --> 00:52:08,458
Your number will appear on the screen when it’s your turn.

871
00:52:08,482 --> 00:52:12,171
I’ll check the screen and wait for my number.

872
00:52:12,195 --> 00:52:15,402
Have you filled out the application form yet?

873
00:52:15,426 --> 00:52:16,892
Yes, you can!

874
00:52:16,915 --> 00:52:20,365
I filled it out at home.

875
00:52:20,389 --> 00:52:25,401
Customer with ticket B-15, please proceed to Window 1.

876
00:52:25,424 --> 00:52:27,897
Window 1, right?

877
00:52:27,920 --> 00:52:30,054
Thank you for your assistance.

878
00:52:30,077 --> 00:52:33,447
This is an application for a renewal of your period of stay, correct?

879
00:52:33,471 --> 00:52:36,160
I’ll take your documents now.

880
00:52:36,183 --> 00:52:41,416
Here’s my application form, passport, and current residence card.

881
00:52:41,439 --> 00:52:44,906
Please submit one passport-sized photo as well.

882
00:52:44,929 --> 00:52:47,262
I’ve prepared the photo.

883
00:52:47,285 --> 00:52:50,019
I wrote my name on the back.

884
00:52:50,042 --> 00:52:54,678
This is a 4cm by 3cm photo, right?

885
00:52:54,701 --> 00:52:56,668
I’ve confirmed it.

886
00:52:56,691 --> 00:52:59,533
Are there any issues with the documents?

887
00:52:59,557 --> 00:53:00,990
Yes, you can!

888
00:53:01,013 --> 00:53:04,980
It’s neatly filled out, so everything looks good.

889
00:53:05,003 --> 00:53:09,502
Can I receive my new residence card today?

890
00:53:09,525 --> 00:53:14,198
Since there will be a review process, you’ll be notified by postcard later.

891
00:53:14,221 --> 00:53:18,588
I’ll come back once the postcard arrives at my home.

892
00:53:18,611 --> 00:53:19,744
Yes, you can!

893
00:53:19,768 --> 00:53:23,101
Please bring the postcard and your passport with you.

894
00:53:23,124 --> 00:53:26,091
How much is the processing fee?

895
00:53:26,114 --> 00:53:31,009
The fee is 4,000 yen, to be paid with revenue stamps.

896
00:53:31,032 --> 00:53:34,052
Where can I buy revenue stamps?

897
00:53:34,075 --> 00:53:37,716
You can buy them at the convenience store on the first floor.

898
00:53:37,740 --> 00:53:41,540
Is there any proof of today’s procedure?

899
00:53:41,563 --> 00:53:47,249
I’ll stamp the back of your residence card to show it’s under renewal.

900
00:53:47,273 --> 00:53:51,473
Does the stamp extend the validity of my card?

901
00:53:51,496 --> 00:53:52,929
Yes, you can!

902
00:53:52,952 --> 00:53:57,285
The validity will be extended for two months until the result is out.

903
00:53:57,308 --> 00:54:00,722
That’s reassuring to hear.

904
00:54:00,746 --> 00:54:04,813
Here’s a copy of your application receipt.

905
00:54:04,836 --> 00:54:07,803
I’ll keep the receipt safe.

906
00:54:07,826 --> 00:54:12,992
The notification postcard usually arrives within two to three weeks.

907
00:54:13,015 --> 00:54:16,549
I’ll check the mailbox every day.

908
00:54:16,572 --> 00:54:20,638
If your address changes, please notify us immediately.

909
00:54:20,661 --> 00:54:22,109
Understood.

910
00:54:22,133 --> 00:54:24,466
My address hasn’t changed.

911
00:54:24,489 --> 00:54:28,489
Today’s application process is now complete.

912
00:54:28,512 --> 00:54:32,046
Thank you for your smooth assistance—it was very helpful.

913
00:54:32,069 --> 00:54:33,635
You’re very welcome.

914
00:54:33,658 --> 00:54:36,658
Please take care on your way home.

915
00:54:36,681 --> 00:54:38,181
Scene 18: Basic Procedures for Moving In

916
00:54:38,181 --> 00:54:42,981
Excuse me, I’d like to complete the moving-in procedures.

917
00:54:43,004 --> 00:54:45,373
Welcome!

918
00:54:45,397 --> 00:54:48,730
Please proceed to the Foreign Residents General Counter.

919
00:54:48,753 --> 00:54:52,353
I’ve just moved to this new city.

920
00:54:52,376 --> 00:54:55,949
Let’s proceed with your moving-in notification.

921
00:54:55,973 --> 00:54:59,806
What documents do I need to fill out?

922
00:54:59,829 --> 00:55:05,605
Please write your new address on this moving-in notification form.

923
00:55:05,629 --> 00:55:08,196
Should I write it in kanji?

924
00:55:08,219 --> 00:55:10,452
Or in romaji?

925
00:55:10,475 --> 00:55:15,342
Please write the address in kanji or with furigana.

926
00:55:15,365 --> 00:55:19,365
Don’t forget to include your apartment room number.

927
00:55:19,388 --> 00:55:23,988
Yes, make sure to write the full address, including the room number.

928
00:55:24,011 --> 00:55:26,977
When did you move in?

929
00:55:27,000 --> 00:55:28,934
It says here.

930
00:55:28,957 --> 00:55:34,523
Please write the date you actually started living at your new address.

931
00:55:34,546 --> 00:55:37,546
I wrote July 20th.

932
00:55:37,569 --> 00:55:42,707
Do you have the moving-out certificate you received from your previous city hall?

933
00:55:42,731 --> 00:55:48,767
Yes, I have my moving-out certificate and residence card.

934
00:55:48,790 --> 00:55:50,557
Thank you.

935
00:55:50,580 --> 00:55:53,946
I’ll take your documents now.

936
00:55:53,969 --> 00:55:58,772
Should I write my new address on the back of my residence card?

937
00:55:58,796 --> 00:56:03,529
Yes, we’ll print your new address on the back.

938
00:56:03,552 --> 00:56:07,927
Do I need to update the address on my My Number Card as well?

939
00:56:07,951 --> 00:56:13,751
Yes, we’ll update the address on your My Number Card at the same time.

940
00:56:13,774 --> 00:56:18,574
Do I need to enter the PIN for my My Number Card?

941
00:56:18,597 --> 00:56:25,564
Yes, please enter your 4-digit PIN on this terminal.

942
00:56:25,587 --> 00:56:28,486
I’ve entered the PIN.

943
00:56:28,509 --> 00:56:32,076
Your card data has been updated.

944
00:56:32,099 --> 00:56:36,232
Can I get a copy of my residence certificate?

945
00:56:36,255 --> 00:56:42,073
Yes, we can issue a residence certificate with your new address.

946
00:56:42,096 --> 00:56:46,063
How much does one copy cost?

947
00:56:46,086 --> 00:56:51,053
A residence certificate costs 300 yen per copy.

948
00:56:51,076 --> 00:56:55,310
I need to submit it to my company, so I’ll take two copies.

949
00:56:55,333 --> 00:56:58,799
That will be 600 yen for two copies.

950
00:56:58,822 --> 00:57:00,920
I'll pay in cash.

951
00:57:00,944 --> 00:57:03,353
Here’s 600 yen.

952
00:57:03,377 --> 00:57:06,344
Thank you, that’s exactly 600 yen.

953
00:57:06,367 --> 00:57:09,533
Here are your two copies of the residence certificate.

954
00:57:09,556 --> 00:57:13,094
Thank you for the quick processing.

955
00:57:13,118 --> 00:57:17,251
I’ll also give you a pamphlet on how to dispose of trash.

956
00:57:17,274 --> 00:57:21,120
Do you have an English version of the pamphlet?

957
00:57:21,144 --> 00:57:25,181
Yes, here’s an English guide to garbage separation.

958
00:57:25,205 --> 00:57:29,971
I’ll make sure to follow the weekday rules for trash disposal.

959
00:57:29,994 --> 00:57:34,594
Please check the collection days, as they vary by area.

960
00:57:34,617 --> 00:57:38,284
Thank you for explaining everything so clearly.

961
00:57:38,307 --> 00:57:42,474
Enjoy your new life in the neighborhood!

962
00:57:42,497 --> 00:57:43,997
Scene 19: Procedure for Receiving My Number Card

963
00:57:43,997 --> 00:57:45,930
Excuse me.

964
00:57:45,953 --> 00:57:49,486
I’d like to receive my My Number Card.

965
00:57:49,509 --> 00:57:51,509
Welcome!

966
00:57:51,533 --> 00:57:54,099
Please proceed to the issuance counter.

967
00:57:54,122 --> 00:57:59,726
I received a pink issuance notice at home.

968
00:57:59,750 --> 00:58:02,753
I’ll take the postcard.

969
00:58:02,776 --> 00:58:05,474
Do you have any identification documents with you?

970
00:58:05,498 --> 00:58:09,564
I have my residence card and passport.

971
00:58:09,587 --> 00:58:11,521
Let me check them.

972
00:58:11,544 --> 00:58:13,910
Your identity has been confirmed.

973
00:58:13,933 --> 00:58:19,067
I’ve already written my name and address on the back of the postcard.

974
00:58:19,090 --> 00:58:22,890
And you’ve signed it as well.

975
00:58:22,913 --> 00:58:24,382
Thank you.

976
00:58:24,405 --> 00:58:28,654
Do I need to set a PIN?

977
00:58:28,677 --> 00:58:32,844
Please set a PIN on your device.

978
00:58:32,867 --> 00:58:36,757
How many types of PINs would you like to set?

979
00:58:36,781 --> 00:58:42,448
We’ll set a 4-digit PIN and an alphanumeric password.

980
00:58:42,471 --> 00:58:48,104
Will the 4-digit PIN be used for certificate issuance at convenience stores?

981
00:58:48,127 --> 00:58:49,461
Yes, you can!

982
00:58:49,484 --> 00:58:53,550
Yes, it’s used when printing your residence certificate at a convenience store.

983
00:58:53,573 --> 00:59:00,540
Now, enter your 4-digit PIN using the keypad on the screen.

984
00:59:00,563 --> 00:59:02,296
I’ve entered it.

985
00:59:02,319 --> 00:59:05,953
Next, we’ll set your alphanumeric password.

986
00:59:05,976 --> 00:59:11,542
Please enter a password between 6 and 16 characters, using letters and numbers.

987
00:59:11,565 --> 00:59:14,998
I’ve entered it with a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters.

988
00:59:15,021 --> 00:59:18,690
Your PIN has been successfully set!

989
00:59:18,714 --> 00:59:24,148
Let’s write down your PIN on this sheet and keep it safe.

990
00:59:24,170 --> 00:59:25,404
Yes, you can!

991
00:59:25,427 --> 00:59:28,673
Please store it carefully so you don’t forget it.

992
00:59:28,697 --> 00:59:33,430
When does my My Number Card expire?

993
00:59:33,453 --> 00:59:38,120
It will expire on the same day as your residence card.

994
00:59:38,143 --> 00:59:41,920
What should I do after renewing my residence card?

995
00:59:41,944 --> 00:59:47,144
Once you renew your residence card, you’ll also need to extend the validity of your My Number Card.

996
00:59:47,167 --> 00:59:51,500
Will I need to visit the ward office again for that?

997
00:59:51,523 --> 00:59:53,004
Yes, you can!

998
00:59:53,028 --> 00:59:57,261
Yes, please come to the ward office before your card expires.

999
00:59:57,284 --> 01:00:00,972
Shall we verify your photo and face?

1000
01:00:00,996 --> 01:00:02,638
Yes, you can!

1001
01:00:02,661 --> 01:00:06,479
We’ll now confirm your identity using the camera on the screen.

1002
01:00:06,503 --> 01:00:09,586
Please remove your mask and look at the screen.

1003
01:00:09,609 --> 01:00:12,209
Identity verification complete.

1004
01:00:12,232 --> 01:00:14,604
Here’s your card.

1005
01:00:14,628 --> 01:00:19,228
Finally, I’ve received my My Number Card!

1006
01:00:19,251 --> 01:00:22,860
You can also use it as your health insurance card.

1007
01:00:22,883 --> 01:00:27,134
It’s so convenient—I can use it when visiting the hospital too!

1008
01:00:27,158 --> 01:00:30,958
Don’t forget to install the Myna Portal app on your smartphone and use it.

1009
01:00:30,981 --> 01:00:34,981
I’ll download the app and start using it.

1010
01:00:35,004 --> 01:00:39,216
If you lose your card, please call us immediately.

1011
01:00:39,239 --> 01:00:42,498
I’ll keep it safely in my wallet.

1012
01:00:42,522 --> 01:00:45,689
Thank you for visiting us today.

1013
01:00:45,712 --> 01:00:47,212
Introduction to Japanese Language Classes

1014
01:00:47,212 --> 01:00:48,818
Excuse me.

1015
01:00:48,841 --> 01:00:52,819
Could you tell me about the Japanese language classes?

1016
01:00:52,842 --> 01:00:54,812
Welcome!

1017
01:00:54,835 --> 01:00:58,314
It’s a volunteer-run Japanese language class.

1018
01:00:58,338 --> 01:01:02,371
Can I study Japanese here?

1019
01:01:02,394 --> 01:01:03,853
Yes,

1020
01:01:03,877 --> 01:01:08,890
Yes, classes are held every Saturday at the community center.

1021
01:01:08,913 --> 01:01:12,485
What time are the classes?

1022
01:01:12,508 --> 01:01:18,542
From 10:00 AM to 11:30 AM—an hour and a half.

1023
01:01:18,566 --> 01:01:21,799
How much is the tuition or participation fee?

1024
01:01:21,822 --> 01:01:25,198
The classes are free!

1025
01:01:25,222 --> 01:01:26,822
Really? Free?

1026
01:01:26,845 --> 01:01:29,478
That’s wonderful!

1027
01:01:29,501 --> 01:01:33,901
You’ll only need to cover the cost of the textbook—500 yen.

1028
01:01:33,924 --> 01:01:36,924
500 yen is very affordable!

1029
01:01:36,947 --> 01:01:40,114
What kind of textbook do you use?

1030
01:01:40,137 --> 01:01:45,737
We use an easy N5-level textbook for beginners.

1031
01:01:45,760 --> 01:01:50,129
Can I start learning hiragana and katakana from scratch?

1032
01:01:50,153 --> 01:01:51,434
Yes,

1033
01:01:51,457 --> 01:01:56,136
We’ll teach you hiragana reading and writing from the very beginning.

1034
01:01:56,160 --> 01:01:59,560
Are you a volunteer teacher?

1035
01:01:59,583 --> 01:02:04,116
Local volunteer teachers will be instructing the classes.

1036
01:02:04,139 --> 01:02:07,739
Can I get one-on-one instruction?

1037
01:02:07,762 --> 01:02:12,540
There will be one teacher for every two students.

1038
01:02:12,563 --> 01:02:16,130
It's a great environment where you can ask plenty of questions.

1039
01:02:16,153 --> 01:02:20,386
You'll get lots of opportunities to practice conversation.

1040
01:02:20,409 --> 01:02:24,018
Can I bring my child along?

1041
01:02:24,042 --> 01:02:25,412
Yes,

1042
01:02:25,436 --> 01:02:30,436
Kids can play in the adjacent kids' space.

1043
01:02:30,459 --> 01:02:35,038
It's reassuring to be able to come with your child.

1044
01:02:35,061 --> 01:02:38,094
We also have childcare volunteers on staff.

1045
01:02:38,118 --> 01:02:40,995
That’s incredibly helpful.

1046
01:02:41,018 --> 01:02:45,290
You can also visit for a tour on Saturday mornings.

1047
01:02:45,314 --> 01:02:49,047
I’d like to come for a tour this Saturday.

1048
01:02:49,070 --> 01:02:50,270
Yes,

1049
01:02:50,293 --> 01:02:53,735
Feel free to drop by for a visit anytime.

1050
01:02:53,759 --> 01:02:57,992
I’ll come this Saturday at 10 AM.

1051
01:02:58,015 --> 01:03:03,349
Please come to our reception desk at 9:45 AM.

1052
01:03:03,372 --> 01:03:07,940
Do I need to fill out the application form now?

1053
01:03:07,963 --> 01:03:12,896
Please provide your name and address by the end of today.

1054
01:03:12,919 --> 01:03:16,523
I’ll write my name and phone number on the form.

1055
01:03:16,547 --> 01:03:18,846
Thank you for filling out the form.

1056
01:03:18,869 --> 01:03:21,477
You’re all set!

1057
01:03:21,501 --> 01:03:25,194
I’m really looking forward to attending the class on Saturday!

1058
01:03:25,218 --> 01:03:29,651
Let’s enjoy learning Japanese together with fellow students!

1059
01:03:29,674 --> 01:03:33,074
I’ll invite my friends to come along too.

1060
01:03:33,097 --> 01:03:36,864
Please feel free to bring your friends!

1061
01:03:36,887 --> 01:03:40,854
Thank you so much for your kind guidance.

1062
01:03:40,878 --> 01:03:43,411
We look forward to seeing you!

1063
01:03:43,434 --> 01:03:45,802
Please take care on your way home.